body:
Thanks, looks good! One more spot with the same root cause: hasNonHexId in src/utils/core.ts still lets an all-hex legacy id through, so getEncodedToken would encode it as hex bytes. Could you add the same length check there (a small isLegacyKeysetId helper might be neat now there are four)?

```ts
// src/crypto/curves.ts
/**
 * True if `keysetId` is a legacy (pre-v1) base64 id, including one that happens to be all hex.
 */
export function isLegacyKeysetId(keysetId: string): boolean {
  return keysetId.length === LEGACY_KEYSET_ID_LENGTH && isBase64String(keysetId);
}

// src/utils/core.ts
function hasNonHexId(proofs: Proof[]) {
  return proofs.some((proof) => !isValidHex(proof.id) || isLegacyKeysetId(proof.id));
}
```
